    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d419">

                <pb facs="0410" n="294" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg294"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 811.34537/108.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                            American Minister</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 169.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-11-15">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">November 15, 1912</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to your No. 477 of the 23d
                    ultimo, I enclose for your information a copy of a letter<anchor n="3"
                        xml:id="d419-f1"/> from the Acting Secretary of the Navy expressing his
                    approval of the final text of the proposed convention for the enlargement of the
                    Guantánamo naval station on the understanding that the rent as proposed by the
                    new agreement covers the entire tract as enlarged.</p>
                <p>Your full powers will be sent to you within a few days, and you may conclude the
                    convention at Habana, either engrossing it at the <pb facs="0411" n="295"
                        xml:id="pg295"/> Legation or requesting the Cuban Foreign Office to engross
                    both copies. You will of course compare the copies, English and Spanish,
                    carefully before signature.</p>
                <p>I am [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">P. C. Knox</hi>.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
